{"type":"message","id":"324072f3","parentId":"c77f27b9","timestamp":"2026-05-24T02:46:02.628Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"With Bearer token I get Unauthorized but with X-API-KEY I get error code 1101. The /health endpoint works with X-API-KEY. The /history endpoint works with X-API-KEY. But /send only works with X-API-KEY and gives error code 1101 regardless of body format.\n\nThis could mean:\n1. The /send endpoint requires additional validation beyond just API key\n2. The error code 1101 might be a custom error meaning something specific\n3. The API key might not have permission to send messages\n\nLet me check if there's a different endpoint or if the platform has some kind of rate limiting or permission system.\n\nLet me try one more thing - maybe the issue is that I'm not providing a valid message format. \n\nI'll test with minimal parameters to see if that changes the response.","thinkingSignature":"fbc1e13ecfc7549ba77643a47b9f5655cead6971515ca90e6aeec8d53e062896"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_1w7f2ux8bo0q_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/keys\" -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_1w7f2ux8bo0q_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"channelId\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"test\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":141,"output":312,"cacheRead":22400,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22853,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779590756463,"responseId":"0661996541dc159fffbee64ae287aca7"}}
